PQ^2 = \frac{169 + 169 + 676}{225} = \frac{1014}{225}
Given that the length of PQ is \(\alpha\), we have \(\alpha^2 = PQ^2\).
\alpha^2 = \frac{1014}{225}

### Step 6: Calculate \(225\alpha^2\)

225\alpha^2 = 225 \times \frac{1014}{225}
\(225\alpha^2 = 1014\)

